## Concepts demonstrated in the project but not yet formally taught

These are concepts the user has *seen* in the code I wrote but hasn't yet
had a lesson on. Each is a candidate for a follow-up `/teach`.

- **Producer/consumer with `condition_variable`** — `LlmClient::workerLoop`.
  Why a CV beats spinning; how `notify_one` vs `notify_all` differ.
- **RAII for thread lifetime** — `LlmClient` ctor starts the thread, dtor
  joins it. What goes wrong if you forget either.
- **Header-only vendored deps** — `external/httplib.h`, `external/json.hpp`.
  When this beats a package manager and when it doesn't.
- **CMake `find_package` vs `target_include_directories`** — the difference
  between a real find module (SFML) and just adding `external/` to the
  include path.
- **System fonts on Linux vs Windows** — the path-probing in
  `findSystemFont()`. Why bundling a font is the alternative.
- **Filesystem path walking with `std::filesystem`** — how `main.cpp`
  locates `config/llm.cfg` whether launched from project root or `build/`.

## Suggested next topic

